  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>In a SHM, mechanical energy is conserved. So, the sum of kinetic energy and potential energy remains constant.</p><p>For a SHM,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">-</mo><mi>U</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>K</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">.</mo><mi>E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>This is the equation of a downward parabola.</p></blockquote>"
